{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Contact

  Shopify's native {% form 'contact' %}, styled to the Shudhi system. Two
  columns: the form on the left, the contact details in a tinted card on the
  right. CSS lives in assets/shudhi-home.css §23 (it replaced §14c, and the
  §15 breakpoint entries moved down with it — a media query adds no
  specificity, so a rule for this component declared in §23 would out-order an
  identical selector left behind in §15 and the layout would never stack).

  Six things here are deliberate and easy to undo by accident:

  1. NEVER pass a custom `id:` to {% form %}. Shopify sets id="contact_form"
     and action="/contact#contact_form" itself, and both the error re-render
     and the ?contact_posted=true redirect jump to that fragment. Overriding
     the id breaks the pairing and the user lands at the top of the page with
     no idea whether anything happened.

  2. [data-reveal] sits on .sh-form__inner, NOT on the <form>. Shopify injects
     form_type and utf8 as the form's first children, so the nth-child ramp in
     §23 would be counting hidden inputs — and would shift silently if Shopify
     ever added a third.

  3. data-reveal is withheld entirely on the success and error renders (see
     `animate_form`, which is computed INSIDE the {% form %} block — `form` is
     scoped to that tag and reading it above the <section> silently compared nil,
     so this guard did nothing at all until that moved).
     The confirmation heading is the autofocus target,
     and moving focus to an element sitting at opacity:0 mid-transform is
     exactly the "motion gates content" failure the house rule forbids. A user
     who just submitted should not have to watch a fade before reading the
     answer either.

  4. No role="status" / role="alert" on the two message blocks. Neither is
     inserted dynamically — both are present at parse time, where a live region
     is either silently ignored or DOUBLE-announces alongside the autofocus.
     One reliable announcement beats two unreliable ones.

  5. The four detail values are normalised ONCE, below, rather than guarded
     four times at the render sites. A value still containing a square bracket
     is a placeholder nobody filled in, and rendering it produced a CLICKABLE
     DEAD LINK (href="tel:[PLACEHOLDER—+9100000000]"). Because the defaults
     lived in two places — this schema and templates/page.contact.json —
     fixing one alone changed nothing. Blanking them here means neither file
     can put a dead link on the page, whatever it holds.

  6. The honeypot CANNOT block a submission. Shopify's native contact form has
     no server-side hook, so a filled trap still sends the email. Its only
     value is as a filter signal: `Website: http://spam.ru` in the notification
     is one inbox rule. Real blocking is Shopify's platform-level reCAPTCHA.
     Anyone reading this as "the theme blocks bots now" is mistaken.

  7. The right column is a WRAPPER (.sh-contact__col--side) holding up to two
     occupants: the details card and the Living Conversation panel. --solo means
     "that column is empty", which is what it always meant — it just used to have
     only one possible occupant. The four combinations:

       panel on,  details empty  -> --lc          55/45, panel centred, full art
       panel on,  details filled -> --lc --both   §23's 1.1fr, card then panel,
                                                  panel compact (no ring, 6 seeds)
       panel off, details filled -> (none)        exactly as before this change
       panel off, details empty  -> --solo        exactly as before this change

     The last two rows are the property to protect: an unconfigured page and a
     details-only page must render byte-identically to what they did before the
     panel existed.

  Custom contact[*] keys (subject, order_number) reach the merchant's
  notification email as humanised "Key: value" lines, but Shopify exposes no
  form.* property for them — so unlike name/email/body they do NOT repopulate
  on the error re-render. That is accepted rather than worked around: the only
  error Shopify actually raises here is an invalid email, and form.body — the
  expensive field to retype — is preserved.

  Heading levels: sh-page-header renders the <h1> above this section, so the
  form heading and the details heading are both h2. The details heading used to
  be a <div>, which filed the whole list under the FORM's heading (WCAG 1.3.1).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}
{%- assign uid = section.id -%}

{%- comment -%} See note 5. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign c_address = s.address | strip -%}
{%- assign c_phone   = s.phone   | strip -%}
{%- assign c_email   = s.email   | strip -%}
{%- assign c_hours   = s.hours   | strip -%}
{%- if c_address contains '[' -%}{%- assign c_address = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if c_phone   contains '[' -%}{%- assign c_phone   = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if c_hours   contains '[' -%}{%- assign c_hours   = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- comment -%} An address is prose; an email is a protocol value. Anything
    without an @ cannot produce a working mailto:, so require the @ rather than
    merely reject the bracket. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless c_email contains '@' -%}{%- assign c_email = '' -%}{%- endunless -%}

{%- comment -%} The old href kept spaces and dots. RFC 3966 tolerates neither
    reliably across dialers. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign tel_href = c_phone | remove: ' ' | remove: '-' | remove: '(' | remove: ')' | remove: '.' -%}

{%- comment -%} With every detail row blank — which is how this ships — the card
    would render as an empty tinted box next to a 500px column of nothing. An
    unconfigured page should look deliberate, not broken, so the aside is
    withheld entirely until it has something to say, and the grid collapses to
    a single measured column (see .sh-contact--solo in §23). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign has_details = false -%}
{%- if c_address != blank or c_phone != blank or c_email != blank or c_hours != blank -%}
  {%- assign has_details = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign has_aside = false -%}
{%- if has_details or s.note != blank -%}
  {%- assign has_aside = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Living Conversation — see note 7.
    Parsed exactly the way reason_options is at :195, and for the same reason:
    `split: '\n'` leaves a \r on every entry pasted from Windows. Emptying the
    statements hides the panel whatever the checkbox says — the same "blank
    content, no element" rule the detail rows use, so the off switch is
    reachable two ways and neither can leave a decorative column with nothing
    in it. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign lc_list = s.lc_statements | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
{%- assign show_panel = false -%}
{%- if s.lc_show and lc_list.size > 0 -%}
  {%- assign show_panel = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} --solo now answers "is the RIGHT COLUMN empty", which is what it
    always meant; it just used to have only one possible occupant. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign has_right = false -%}
{%- if has_aside or show_panel -%}
  {%- assign has_right = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

<section class="sh sh-contact{% unless has_right %} sh-contact--solo{% endunless %}{% if show_panel %} sh-contact--lc{% endif %}{% if show_panel and has_aside %} sh-contact--both{% endif %}" id="contact"{% if s.bg != blank %} style="--sh-contact-bg:{{ s.bg }};"{% endif %}>
  <div class="sh-wrap">
    <div class="sh-contact__grid">

      {%- comment -%} Form {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="sh-contact__col--form">
        {%- form 'contact', class: 'sh-form' -%}
          {%- comment -%} INSIDE the form block, and that is the whole point.
              `form` is a Liquid object Shopify creates for the {% form %} tag
              and it does not exist outside it — so computing this above the
              <section>, where it used to live, silently evaluated
              form.posted_successfully? and form.errors against nil. The unless
              therefore always passed and animate_form was simply `s.animate`.

              Verified in the browser before this change: on
              /pages/contact?contact_posted=true the confirmation rendered AND
              .sh-form__inner still carried data-reveal — the exact failure note 3
              describes as forbidden, in the file that documents it. The
              confirmation heading is the autofocus target, so focus was landing
              on an element at opacity:0 mid-transform.

              Liquid `assign` writes to the template scope, not a block-local one
              ({% form %} is not a loop), so both variables are still readable
              after {% endform %} — which is where the right column needs them.
              The form column renders BEFORE that column, so the order holds.
              {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign animate_form = false -%}
          {%- if s.animate -%}
            {%- unless form.posted_successfully? or form.errors -%}
              {%- assign animate_form = true -%}
            {%- endunless -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%} The panel's opening line and status are printed from
              this server-side, so both are right with JS off and neither can
              ever claim a success the form did not have. {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign lc_state = 'idle' -%}
          {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
            {%- assign lc_state = 'sent' -%}
          {%- elsif form.errors -%}
            {%- assign lc_state = 'error' -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          <div class="sh-form__inner"{% if animate_form %} data-reveal{% endif %}>

            {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
              {%- comment -%} tabindex/autofocus: see note 3. autofocus has been a
                  global HTML attribute since 2019, so this needs no JS. Browsers
                  that ignore it degrade to the previous behaviour exactly. {%- endcomment -%}
              <h2 class="sh-contact__title sh-serif" tabindex="-1" autofocus>{{ s.success_title }}</h2>

              <p class="sh-form__ok">
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'leaf' %}
                <span>{{ s.success_text }}</span>
              </p>

              {%- if s.success_link != blank and s.success_link_label != blank -%}
                <p class="sh-form__after">
                  <a class="sh-btn sh-btn--ghost" href="{{ s.success_link }}">
                    {{ s.success_link_label }}{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
                  </a>
                </p>
              {%- endif -%}

            {%- else -%}
              {%- if s.form_title != blank -%}
                <h2 class="sh-contact__title sh-serif">{{ s.form_title }}</h2>
              {%- endif -%}

              {%- if form.errors -%}
                <div class="sh-form__err" tabindex="-1" autofocus>
                  {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'alert' %}
                  <div>
                    {%- if s.error_title != blank -%}
                      <p class="sh-form__err-title">{{ s.error_title }}</p>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{ form.errors | default_errors }}
                  </div>
                </div>
              {%- elsif s.form_lede != blank -%}
                <p class="sh-form__lede">{{ s.form_lede }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}

              <div class="sh-form__body">
                <div class="sh-form__row">
                  <div class="sh-field">
                    <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-name-{{ uid }}">
                      {{ s.label_name }}<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                    </label>
                    <input type="text" id="sh-name-{{ uid }}" name="contact[name]"
                           required aria-required="true" autocomplete="name"
                           value="{{ form.name | default: customer.name }}">
                  </div>

                  <div class="sh-field">
                    <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-email-{{ uid }}">
                      {{ s.label_email }}<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                    </label>
                    <input type="email" id="sh-email-{{ uid }}" name="contact[email]"
                           required aria-required="true" autocomplete="email"
                           value="{{ form.email | default: customer.email }}">
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="sh-form__row">
                  <div class="sh-field">
                    <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-phone-{{ uid }}">{{ s.label_phone }}</label>
                    <input type="tel" id="sh-phone-{{ uid }}" name="contact[phone]" autocomplete="tel">
                  </div>

                  {%- if s.show_order -%}
                    <div class="sh-field">
                      <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-order-{{ uid }}">{{ s.label_order }}</label>
                      <input type="text" id="sh-order-{{ uid }}" name="contact[order_number]"
                             inputmode="numeric"
                             {% if s.hint_order != blank %}aria-describedby="sh-order-hint-{{ uid }}"{% endif %}>
                      {%- if s.hint_order != blank -%}
                        <p class="sh-field__hint" id="sh-order-hint-{{ uid }}">{{ s.hint_order }}</p>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>

                {%- comment -%} Blank reason_options drops the field entirely — the
                    same "blank content = no element" rule the detail rows use.
                    The first line is pre-selected, so the email always carries a
                    meaningful value without a required-select failure mode. {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign reasons = s.reason_options | strip | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
                {%- if reasons.size > 0 -%}
                  <div class="sh-field">
                    <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-reason-{{ uid }}">{{ s.label_reason }}</label>
                    <select id="sh-reason-{{ uid }}" name="contact[subject]">
                      {%- for r in reasons -%}
                        {%- assign r = r | strip -%}
                        {%- if r != blank -%}
                          <option value="{{ r | escape }}">{{ r }}</option>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </select>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}

                <div class="sh-field">
                  <label class="sh-field__label" for="sh-body-{{ uid }}">
                    {{ s.label_message }}<span class="sh-field__req" aria-hidden="true">*</span>
                  </label>
                  <textarea id="sh-body-{{ uid }}" name="contact[body]" rows="6"
                            required aria-required="true">{{ form.body }}</textarea>
                </div>

                {%- comment -%} See note 6. Offset off-screen, not display:none —
                    bots skip hidden fields but fill offset ones. tabindex="-1" is
                    load-bearing: it keeps the field out of the tab order, which is
                    what lets the aria-hidden wrapper pass axe's aria-hidden-focus
                    rule (that rule flags TABBABLE content inside aria-hidden). {%- endcomment -%}
                <div class="sh-form__hp" aria-hidden="true">
                  <label for="sh-website-{{ uid }}">Do not fill this in</label>
                  <input type="text" id="sh-website-{{ uid }}" name="contact[website]"
                         tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" value="">
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="sh-form__actions">
                <button type="submit" class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid">
                  {{ s.submit_label }}{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
                </button>
                {%- if s.privacy_note != blank -%}
                  <p class="sh-form__privacy">{{ s.privacy_note }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

          </div>
        {%- endform -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Right column. The wrapper exists so the details card and
          the panel can share the column; .sh-contact__col--info sets no
          grid-placement properties, so moving it one level down changes nothing
          about how it renders, and its own data-reveal and nth-child ramp
          (§23 :2921) are untouched.

          Card first, panel second. The card is information someone came here
          for; the panel is atmosphere. Fact above motion — and it keeps the
          moving parts out of the top of the reading path. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if has_right -%}
      <div class="sh-contact__col--side">

      {%- comment -%} Details {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if has_aside -%}
      <aside class="sh-contact__col--info"{% if s.animate %} data-reveal{% endif %}>
        {%- if has_details -%}
        <div class="sh-contact__card">
          {%- if s.info_title != blank -%}
            <h2 class="sh-contact__eyebrow">{{ s.info_title }}</h2>
            <i class="sh-contact__rule" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          {%- endif -%}

          <dl class="sh-contact__list">
            {%- if c_address != blank -%}
              <div class="sh-contact__item">
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'pin' %}
                <div>
                  <dt>Visit</dt>
                  <dd>
                    {{ c_address }}
                    {%- if s.map_url != blank -%}
                      <a class="sh-contact__map" href="{{ s.map_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                        Get directions{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
                      </a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </dd>
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if c_phone != blank -%}
              <div class="sh-contact__item">
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'phone' %}
                <div>
                  <dt>Call</dt>
                  <dd><a href="tel:{{ tel_href }}">{{ c_phone }}</a></dd>
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if c_email != blank -%}
              <div class="sh-contact__item">
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'mail' %}
                <div>
                  <dt>Email</dt>
                  <dd><a href="mailto:{{ c_email }}">{{ c_email }}</a></dd>
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if c_hours != blank -%}
              <div class="sh-contact__item">
                {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'clock' %}
                <div><dt>Hours</dt><dd>{{ c_hours }}</dd></div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </dl>
        </div>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.note != blank -%}
          <p class="sh-contact__note">{{ s.note }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      </aside>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%} `animate: animate_form` is note 3 applied a second time —
          ONE flag, two consumers. On the success and error renders it is false,
          so the panel ships without data-reveal and sits still while the
          autofocused confirmation heading is the only thing moving. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if show_panel -%}
        {%- render 'sh-living-conversation',
              uid: uid, s: s, lc_list: lc_list,
              animate: animate_form, lc_state: lc_state, compact: has_aside -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{%- comment -%} Emitted from the section, not from layout/theme.liquid, and not
    behind a template check. This section ships a preset, so a merchant can add
    the form to ANY page — a `template.name == 'page' and template.suffix ==
    'contact'` gate would gate the wrong thing, and a looser `template contains
    'contact'` also matches page.contactus, page.contact-us-v2 and
    page.contact-us-v3, three templates that do not render this section at all.

    `defer` is honoured on a parser-inserted classic script anywhere in the
    document, so this still runs after parsing and after shudhi-home.js (head,
    defer, earlier in document order). Two sh-contact sections on one page would
    emit this twice: the browser fetches once but EXECUTES twice, which is what
    the window.__shLC re-entry guard at the top of the file answers. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- if show_panel -%}
  <script src="{{ 'sh-living-conversation.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Contact",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "form_title", "label": "Form heading", "default": "Send us a message" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "form_lede", "label": "Form intro",
      "info": "Sets expectations before the first field, and is where the required-field legend lives. Blank hides it.",
      "default": "Tell us what you need and we'll reply personally, usually within two working days. Fields marked * are required." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Form fields" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_name", "label": "Name label", "default": "Name" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_email", "label": "Email label", "default": "Email address" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_phone", "label": "Phone label", "default": "Phone" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_reason", "label": "Reason label", "default": "What's this about?" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "reason_options", "label": "Reason options",
      "info": "One per line. The first line is pre-selected. Leave blank to drop the field entirely. Arrives in your notification email as \"Subject\".",
      "default": "General enquiry\nProduct advice\nOrder or delivery\nReturn or exchange\nBulk order enquiry\nPress and collaborations" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_order", "label": "Ask for an order number", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_order", "label": "Order number label", "default": "Order number" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hint_order", "label": "Order number hint",
      "default": "Optional. Speeds up anything to do with a delivery." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "label_message", "label": "Message label", "default": "Your message" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "submit_label", "label": "Button text", "default": "Send message" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "privacy_note", "label": "Privacy line",
      "info": "Sits under the button. Blank hides it.",
      "default": "We use your details only to answer this message." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "After sending",
      "info": "The confirmation replaces the form and takes keyboard focus, so it has to read as a complete answer on its own." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_title", "label": "Confirmation heading", "default": "Your message is on its way" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "success_text", "label": "Confirmation text",
      "default": "Thank you — we've received it and usually reply within two working days. Do check your spam folder if you don't hear from us." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "success_link", "label": "Confirmation link",
      "info": "Optional. Gives the confirmation somewhere to go instead of dead-ending." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "success_link_label", "label": "Confirmation link text", "default": "Continue shopping" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "error_title", "label": "Error heading", "default": "We couldn't send that yet" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Contact details",
      "info": "Any row left blank is hidden. A value that still contains a square bracket is treated as unfilled and hidden too, so a half-configured page never renders a dead tel: or mailto: link." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "info_title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Get in touch" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "address", "label": "Address", "info": "Street, city, state, PIN." },
    { "type": "url", "id": "map_url", "label": "Directions link",
      "info": "Optional. Adds a \"Get directions\" link under the address." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "phone", "label": "Phone",
      "info": "Write it the way you want it read, e.g. +91 98765 43210. The tel: link is built from it." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "email", "label": "Email", "info": "Must contain an @, or the row is hidden." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "hours", "label": "Hours", "info": "e.g. Mon–Sat, 10am–6pm IST." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "note", "label": "Footnote",
      "info": "Optional. Do not use it to ask for an order number — there is a field for that now." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Living conversation panel",
      "info": "The editorial panel beside the form. Emptying \"Rotating statements\" hides it whatever the checkbox says — the same rule the detail rows follow. Write everything below in sentence case; the panel sets it in capitals itself." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "lc_show", "label": "Show the panel", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "A conversation" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lc_statements", "label": "Rotating statements",
      "info": "One per line. The first line shows before anything else happens, then they cycle in this order.",
      "default": "Good things begin with a conversation.\nLet's create something meaningful.\nEvery ritual begins somewhere.\nWe'd love to hear from you.\nTake your time. We're listening.\nRooted in nature. Made for you." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_support", "label": "Supporting line",
      "default": "Tell us what you're looking for. We'll take it from there." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "lc_interval", "label": "Between statements",
      "min": 4, "max": 12, "step": 1, "unit": "s", "default": 7 },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Living conversation — while filling the form",
      "info": "Shown while the matching field is in use. Leave any blank to keep the rotating statements running for that field." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_name", "label": "Name field", "default": "Let's start with your name." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_email", "label": "Email field", "default": "Where can we reach you?" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_phone", "label": "Phone field", "default": "We'll keep it simple." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_order", "label": "Order number field", "default": "We'll help you find your order." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_reason", "label": "Reason field", "default": "Tell us where to start." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_message", "label": "Message field", "default": "Take your time. We're listening." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_typing", "label": "After a few words", "default": "We're listening." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_typing_2", "label": "After a sentence", "default": "Every word matters." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "lc_on_typing_3", "label": "After a paragraph", "default": "Thank you for sharing." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Living conversation — after sending",
